diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8347b4a..2e3e1bd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,32 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and on every pushed tag
+matching `v*`. It can also be started manually (`workflow_dispatch`).
 
 This repository is public.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow assumes `arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in
+`eu-north-1` through GitHub OIDC. No long-lived AWS access keys are stored;
+the `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` secrets are no longer used
+and should be deleted from the repository settings.
+
+The role's trust policy must allow `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` and
+match `sub` exactly, with no wildcards. Branch and tag runs have different
+subjects, so list both:
+
+- `repo:OWNER/REPO:ref:refs/heads/main`
+- `repo:OWNER/REPO:ref:refs/tags/v*` (use `StringLike` for this one only)
+
+Prefer a GitHub environment and match `repo:OWNER/REPO:environment:NAME`
+if you want a required-reviewer gate on deployments.
+
+## Runner
+
+Jobs run on GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-latest`. Self-hosted runners are not used
+because the repository is public.
+
+## Notifications
+
+A Slack message is sent at the end of each run using the `SLACK_WEBHOOK` secret.
